# Feature-sliced design (`src/shared`)

All FSD layers live under `src/shared/` (the AppBuilderShared submodule). Alias `@AppBuilderLib/` → `src/shared/`. Host code in `src/webgi/` and `src/AppBuilder*.tsx` is **not** FSD.

| Layer | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `shared/` | Reusable code with no business logic (ui, lib, config) |
| `entities/` | Business entities (session, parameter, viewport types, …) |
| `features/` | User-facing features with business logic |
| `widgets/` | Composite UI blocks |
| `pages/` | Full page compositions |

Segments: `ui/` (React), `model/` (zustand/hooks), `api/`, `lib/` (pure), `config/` (types/constants).

Cross-slice imports: `@AppBuilderLib/{layer}/{slice}/{segment}/{file}`. Intra-slice: relative. Do **not** create new slice `index.ts` barrels; import concrete modules. This host already uses deep imports to avoid pulling `@shapediver/viewer.features.*`.

## Migration

If asked to migrate a file into FSD: show a FROM/TO plan and **wait for confirmation**. Move with `git -C src/shared mv` (never copy+delete). Update all imports. One file at a time. Preserve filenames.
